2 CONT     "Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island", by John Osborne Austin, (Genealogical Publishing Co. Inc.,) Baltimore, Maryland, 1969,1978,1982,1995), Page 97:
2 CONT
2 CONT     "1679 May 8" Thomas Hicks sold a quarter share at Seaconnet to Lawrence Springer, for 22 pds. 10 shillings."
2 CONT
2 CONT     "Rhode Island Land Evidences, Vol. I, 1648-1696" by Dorothy Worthington, Rhode Island:
2 CONT
2 CONT     On June 23, 1679, Lawrence Springer sold 1/8 part of a share of land (the 3 and 20th lot) in Sakonnet, Little Compton, Newport Co., RI to Robert Gibbs for 12 pounds sterling.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Bristol County, Probate Court, Book 2, Page 33:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Will: Sept. 4, 1701 Probate: Feb. 2, 1701-2
2 CONT
2 CONT     To Martha Springer my wife use of whole estate during her life, housing, land, good and chattel and after her death to my two sons Thomas & Edward Springer who shall have all housing and lands m goods and chattels equally....
2 CONT
2 CONT     To Son John Springer 5 pds.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To Son Jonathan Springer 5 pds.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To Son Benjamin Springer 5 pds.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To Son Joseph Springer 5 pds.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To son Henry Springer 5 pds.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To daughters Mary Weaver, Joanna Springer, Martha Springer 40 shillings each.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To daughter Mary's eldest daughter called Ann Dier and daughter Joanna's
2 CONT
2 CONT     eldest son Jeremiah a yearling calf between them.
2 CONT
2 CONT     To friends John Wilbore senr, and Joseph Wilbore overseers of this my will.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Witnesses
2 CONT
2 CONT     David Hillard
2 CONT
2 CONT     James Bennett
2 CONT
2 CONT     Nathaniel Searles
2 CONT
2 CONT     On Nov. 16, 1703 John and Joseph Wilbore applied to the court for permission to terminate their administration of the will, as Lawrence, the youngest son had come of age.
