2 CONT
2 CONT     "The Durfee family were from Tiverton, RI In the Summer o
2 CONT
2 CONT     f 1790, Gideon and Edward came first to Farmington, and Gid
2 CONT
2 CONT     eon returned in the fall representing the country so favora
2 CONT
2 CONT     bly, that the whole family resolved upon emigration. Gideo
2 CONT
2 CONT     n with Isaac Springer, came back in the winter of 1790 an
2 CONT
2 CONT     d 91 with an ox sled, consuming 17 1/2 days in the journey
2 CONT
2 CONT     . Gideon purchased of John Swift his choice of 1,600 acres
2 CONT
2 CONT     . He located it on what was long known as "Durfee street
2 CONT
2 CONT     " a short distance below Palmyra, securing a large amount o
2 CONT
2 CONT     f the flats on the Ganargeva; Being soon rejoined by his br
2 CONT
2 CONT     other Edward, the brother and Springer built a cabin and cl
2 CONT
2 CONT     earing six acres, and without the use of a plough, plante
2 CONT
2 CONT     d it to corn.
