1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.nojesdans.se/marika/familj/lena/index.html#50
2 CONT
2 CONT G 20 dec 1832 i Sthlm, Kat, m Hulda Philippina Forsström, f 22 aug 1813 i Gustavia, Saint-Barthélemy, Västindien, d 15 aug 1888 i Sthlm, Hedv El, dtr till kontraktsprosten kh Johan Eric F o Petronella Elisabeth Robertson.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/Sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=9518
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Erik Forsström (1775–1824) was a Swedish pastor and naturalist from the province of Dalarna. The plant genus Forsstroemia from the family Leptodontaceae is named after him.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He studied at the University of Uppsala, where one of his instructors was naturalist Carl Peter Thunberg (1743–1828). In 1800, he accompanied Göran Wahlenberg (1780–1851) on an expedition through Fennoscandia, where he performed e
2 CONC ntomological and botanical investigations. On the trip he maintained a journal, and in 1917 details of the expedition were published in a book titled I Norrlandsstäder och Lapplandsbygd År 1800. John Erik Forsströms dagbok öfver r
2 CONC esan i Norrland och Finnmarken 1800 och i Roslagen 1801.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1802 until 1815, Forsström was assigned as pastor in Saint Barthélemy of the Leeward Islands, where he also worked collecting botanical specimens. Afterwards he returned to Sweden, where he died in 1824 at Munktorp, located n
2 CONC ear the town of Köping.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Erik_Forsstr%C3%B6m
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.myheritage.se/research/collection-1/myheritage-slakttrad?itemId=264647171-3-500988&action=showRecord&recordTitle=Jan+Eric+Mattiasson
